description:
Build the byte pattern tools of lesson 4.05:

```cpp
using Pattern = std::vector<std::optional<std::uint8_t>>;

std::optional<Pattern> parsePattern(const std::string& text);
std::vector<std::size_t> findAll(const std::vector<std::uint8_t>& bytes, const Pattern& pattern);
std::optional<std::uint64_t> ripTarget(const std::vector<std::uint8_t>& bytes, std::size_t instruction, std::size_t length,
                                        std::size_t displacementAt, std::uint64_t base);
```

- **parsePattern** reads tokens separated by spaces: two hex digits (either case) for a byte, `??` or `?` for a wildcard. Anything else, or no tokens at all, gives `std::nullopt`.
- **findAll** returns every offset where the pattern matches, in order (matches may overlap).
- **ripTarget**: the instruction at offset `instruction` of `bytes` (loaded at address `base`) is `length` bytes long and holds a signed 32-bit displacement at byte `displacementAt` of the instruction. Return the address it refers to: the address just past the instruction plus the displacement. If the bytes run out, return `std::nullopt`.

